   "text": {
    "L1": "Mr Raven sat on a tree limb with a morsel in his beak.",
    "L2": "The fox praised him to make him proud and get the food.",
    "L3": "The raven believed the praise and forgot that his voice was only a croak.",
    "L4": "When he opened his beak to sing, the morsel fell and the fox took it.",
    "L5": "The poem teaches us not to be fooled by sweet words or pride.",
    "L6": "Honest praise is specific and has no hidden demand. Flattery exaggerates and wants something in return.",
    "L7": "The poem rhymes in couplets. For example, beak rhymes with seek.",
    "L8": "Now tap the message that is flattery."
   },
